    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass with a green build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same first and last name, case-insensitively.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount.java` counts existing owners (`ownerRepository.findAll()`) whose `firstName` and `lastName` match the new owner case-insensitively, excluding the not-yet-persisted owner, and stores the snapshot on the entity. It sits between `assignHousehold` and `save` in `owners.POST.yml` (added under the same `transaction` governance), so the count reflects state *before* this create and is captured before the row is written.\n\n2. **Persistence** \u2014 added a `namesakeCount` field (`namesake_count` column) to the `Owner` entity, since the value is read back later via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and `ddl-auto=none` for the test DB. Added the column to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n3. **API/DTO** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (generates `OwnerDto`); it maps automatically Owner\u2192OwnerDto by name, and I added the matching `@Mapping(ignore)` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` in `OwnerMapper`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCountsNamesakes` passes (creates two owners with the same name but different addresses \u2192 second owner's `namesakeCount` = 1), and the full suite (260 tests) stays green.",
